      "proposed_content": "The 1936 higher-genus program replaced elliptic endomorphisms by self-correspondences but still lacked a theory of differentials and a norm generalization leading to positive definiteness; the mature finite-field picture forces the equivalent sign through an intersection-form index theorem, while the classical problem still lacks corresponding cohomology, Frobenius, and an index theorem.",
