    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8b864cecc8b8dcb52f6bb072de4e0d514d171a339f209cd93781732274cf98ce",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Hilbert-Polya requires a natural Hermitian operator whose eigenvalues are the zero ordinates, whereas the Veneziano construction supplies an equivalent integral identity and only conjectures an effective Riemann string; independently, a quantum-state overlap can approximate zeta accurately even when its Hamiltonian fails termwise to approximate the intended logarithmic spectrum.",
