      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The Gram test supplied cheap critical-line intervals, but empty intervals were compensated by extra zeros nearby and failures clustered; Lehmer therefore used an explicit remainder bound to route ambiguous or failed intervals to subdivision and a sharper formula, while modern verification stops refining a zero as soon as a rigorous sign-change count is secured.",
